  "prompt": "How many days remain to file the individual income tax return?",
  "runtimeCommit": "ba08ae790021ac1e22f438a82372a643dd886de0",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline to file the individual income tax return in the Philippines is typically on April 15 of the following year after the taxable year.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should ensure that their returns are filed by this deadline to avoid penalties and interest on any unpaid taxes. It is advisable to prepare and submit the return well in advance of the deadline to account for any potential issues that may arise during the filing process.",
